Licence for the data
====================

The SOFTWARE in this repository is under the MIT licence; see LICENSE.

The DATA it produces — the CSV export in `data/`, the RDF in `rdf/`, the
published graph at `docs/bundle.ttl`, and the figures in `img/` — are made
available under

    Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Two licences rather than one, on purpose: a permissive code licence says
nothing about who may reuse the archaeological record that the code
processes, and a reader of the graph should not have to infer the terms
from the terms on the software.

Attribution
-----------

    Samian Research Community (year): Archaeological findspots dated by
    samian potters' stamps. Leibniz-Zentrum für Archäologie (LEIZA).
    https://github.com/leiza-rse/IPSDatedSites

Cite the dated snapshot, not an individual findspot. Findspot and
time-span URIs are deliberately not versioned: they denote the same
findspot permanently, and their values change when the source data are
improved. The dataset node carries `dcterms:issued` and `owl:versionInfo`
for exactly this purpose.

Machine-readable
----------------

The same statement is in the graph itself, on the dataset node:

    dcterms:license   <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>
    dcterms:creator   "Samian Research Community"
    dcterms:publisher "Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Archaeologie (LEIZA)"
    dcat:contactPoint "Dr. Allard W. Mees, ..."

so an aggregator can read the terms off the data without consulting this
file.

Source data
-----------

Derived from the Samian Research / Index Professionum Signorum (IPS)
database. Rights in the source database are held by its publishers and are
independent of both licences above.

